<https://id.dalia.education/learning-resource/e90f78ac-93f3-4d59-9d16-0ab429723e23> a ec:EducationalResource ;
    bflr:supportinghost dalia-community:aac7b1be-cf00-4fdc-a26a-e8e0e1410b18 ;
    dcterms:description "Taxonomic Harmonization: A problem you didn’t know you had! A lecture given in the context of the first GfÖ &amp; NFDI4Biodiversity Winter School on Data Management in Ecology and Environmental Science December 5-9, 2022. This lecture aims to be an introduction to the problem of taxonomic harmonization and how to solve it. It's organized into four sections: What is taxonomy? (Taxonomy 101) What is “taxonomic harmonization”? What is needed to perform taxonomic harmonization? How to perform taxonomic harmonization in practice? It's following the CC-BY 4.0 License It heavily relies on the following publication, please cite it if you use some of the material: Grenié, M., Berti, E., Carvajal-Quintero, J., Dädlow, G. M., Sagouis, A. &amp; Winter, M. (2022). Harmonizing taxon names in biodiversity data: A review of tools, databases and best practices. <em>Methods in Ecology and Evolution</em>, 00, 1– 14. https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.13802 An up-to-date version of this material is also available on GitHub: https://github.com/Rekyt/taxonomic_harmonization_lecture" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-3/eng> ;
    dcterms:license <http://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dcterms:title "Taxonomic Harmonization" ;
    rec:recommender dalia-community:aac7b1be-cf00-4fdc-a26a-e8e0e1410b18 ;
    fabio:hasDiscipline <https://w3id.org/kim/hochschulfaechersystematik/n026> ;
    fabio:hasSubtitle "a problem you didn't know you had!" ;
    ns1:authorUnordered [ a schema:Person ;
            m4i:orcidId "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4659-7522" ;
            schema:familyName "Grenié" ;
            schema:givenName "Matthias" ] ;
